number: 2390

title: Inform AI of host OS for execute_shell

body (full text, not truncated):

### ⚠️ Search for existing issues first ⚠️

- [X] I have searched the existing issues, and there is no existing issue for my problem

### GPT-3 or GPT-4

- [ ] I am using Auto-GPT with GPT-3 (GPT-3.5)

### Steps to reproduce 🕹

This issue relates and expands issue #2257 

Configuration: 
- AutoGPT stable version v0.2.1
- Windows 10 Pro 22H2
- miniconda with Python 3.10.9
- all requirements installed
- full prompt provided below

### Current behavior 😯

AutoGPT doesn't check the host OS on startup and tries to execute Linux bash commands on a Windows machine. That includes using the wrong path separator (as reported in issue #2257). In doing so it's unable to create nested subfolders ('projectname\data') and at times but not always, unable to save python files with the correct line termination.

Example line below:
NEXT ACTION:  COMMAND = execute_shell ARGUMENTS = {'command_line': 'mkdir -p wine-quality/wget && cd wine-quality/wget && wget https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/wget/wget-1.21.2.tar.gz && tar -xvf wget-1.21.2.tar.gz && cd wget-1.21.2 && ./configure && make && make install && echo "export PATH=$PATH:/usr/local/bin" >> ~/.bashrc && source ~/.bashrc'}

### Expected behavior 🤔

Be aware of the host OS and use compatible syntax and commands.

### Your prompt 📝

ai_goals:
- Create the working directory 'wine-quality', download any .csv dataset from https://archive.ics.uci.edu/ml/machine-learning-databases/wine-quality/ and save them in the folder 'wine-quality\data'
- Import the csv datasets and use the last column as output
- Develop the most accurate machine learning model using TensorFlow and Keras to maximise the
  output accuracy. Any model training and testing should be executed locally and not using cloud-based virtual machines
- Write a Jupyter notebook including all code to import datasets, set up the best model
  found in previous step and presenting results both numerically and graphically.
  The jupyter notebook should be saved under the folder 'wine-quality\output'
ai_name: Wine tester
ai_role: An AI to autonomously improve wine detection results from a well-known dataset.
  Any python file required to achieve the goal should be saved in the folder 'wine-quality'
  and any dataset stored locally under the folder 'wine-quality\data'


